    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nnew, mini.snippets\n\n### Description\n\n**Idea**: Allow snippets defined via lua to add callback functions that allow to add dynamic logic to snippets.\n\n**Example use-case**: I want to create a snippet that creates a python class:\n```python\nclass MyClass:\n  def __init__(self, $1, ...)\n    $0\n```\nAfter hitting $0, I would like to run lua code that captures all the arguments provided and adds a body to the python function, e.g.\n```python\nclass MyClass:\n  def __init__(self, arg: int, arg2: str, arg3: str = \"str\", ...)\n    self.arg = arg  # dynamically generated after finishing the snippet\n    self.arg1 = arg1\n    self.arg2 = arg2\n    self.arg3 = arg3\n```\n\nI like to imagine that this would be quite easy with a callback function that is executed at the end of snippet creation. It also seems very much in line with the design of other modules.",
