            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nFor this type of use case there are [dedicated events](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/0a9259e95dbfcd07d5d506c56afd615e018acc4e/doc/mini-snippets.txt#L1091-L1104) and here `MiniSnippetsSessionStop` seems relevant. The `data` field of autocommand table arguments contains `session` field which can be used to extract information for the stopped session.\n\nClosing as it seems already be possible.",
